  - name: "Art of Evasion (Hsing Tsia)"
    description: "Mystic Art of Invisibility: staying out of view behind someone, turning as he turns. Automatic if the enemy is unaware; if he knows or suspects, 50% +3% per level. The character can keep attacking from behind while unseen. Fails if a companion of the victim can see and warn him or the victim backs against a wall; only the victim is fooled, and once he sees the stalker the power is negated."
  - name: "Art of Vanishing (Sun Shih K''an Chien Chih)"
    description: "Mystic Art of Invisibility: disappearing from clear view, even mid-combat, by distraction and a sudden drop or roll. 85% +1% per level in full darkness with many obstructions; cumulative penalties of -10% in fair light, -20% in strong light, -15% on clear, flat, featureless ground, and -20% when cornered. Lasts one melee action and counts as one melee action."
  - name: "Art of Disguise (Hensho-Jutsu)"
    description: "Mystic Art of Invisibility: instantly changing posture, walk and expression to become unrecognizable. Automatic in crowds of 100 or more; otherwise 50% +3% per level, -40% if stopped and specifically questioned or searched. Combined with the Disguise skill: 96% to conceal true identity and 88% to impersonate a specific person or occupation (after hours of study)."
  - name: "Art of Mystic Invisibility (Chi Zoshiki)"
    description: "Mystic Art of Invisibility: clouding the minds of observers to vanish even in full view. Costs 1 P.P.E. per melee round for one observer, 4 per round for 2-8 people, 12 per round for more than eight. The character must turn visible to fight or use skills other than the arts of invisibility. It also shields his P.P.E. from detection and siphoning, and those clouded cannot see him with optics or motion detectors. Save: 19 or higher, one roll for a group. May try once per melee round."
  - name: "Zenjoriki: Calm Minds"
    description: "10 P.P.E., 120 feet, three minutes: everyone in range, friend or foe, who fails a save of 17 (M.E. bonus applies) stops attacking, though they may defend or flee; any attack by the user ends it, and it cannot be used on the same group again for an hour. It also dispels fear and hysteria."
  - name: "Zenjoriki: Karumi-Jutsu"
    description: "10 P.P.E., self, three minutes per level: controls the body''s weight while concentrating, to fall any distance unhurt, jump ten times the normal distance, climb any surface like an insect, and tread on the most delicate surfaces without harm. It does not work in combat."
  - name: "Zenjoriki: Two Minds"
    description: "30 P.P.E., self, three minutes per level: the soul splits into the analytical Hun, a ghostly form with the mental skills and magic or psionics, and the instinctive Po, which keeps the body and fights with every physical skill but cannot speak or think tactically. Hit points and S.D.C. are split between them, and the roles cannot be swapped until they rejoin."
  - name: "Zenjoriki: Vibrating Palm"
    description: "70 P.P.E., 120 feet, up to 10 melee rounds: sympathetic vibrations shatter an object or being, 1 point in the first round and doubling each round to a maximum of 512 by the tenth; S.D.C. against S.D.C. targets and M.D. against mega-damage ones. It takes the user''s complete attention, and any interruption resets it."
  - name: "Zenjoriki: Vital Strike Atemi"
    description: "20 P.P.E., touch: a punch, kick or hand-weapon strike does its normal damage directly to hit points, and a victim reduced to zero falls into a coma whatever S.D.C. remains; a roll with impact that beats the strike halves it. Against mega-damage supernatural beings it does the blow''s damage x2 as M.D. It cannot pass environmental armor."
  - name: "Zenjoriki: Withering Flesh Atemi"
    description: "25 P.P.E. on a hit, 5 on a miss; punch or kick: instead of normal damage the strike strips up to 100 of the victim''s natural S.D.C., leaving hit points exposed; a roll with impact that beats the strike halves it. Against mega-damage supernatural beings it does 2D4x10 M.D. (1D4x10 against elementals), up to half the creature''s M.D.C., and that damage cannot regenerate for an hour."
  - name: "Magic (adults and NPC dragons)"
